  "findings": "Compared the irregular multi-shoot woodland understorey habit and leathery elliptic leaf photograph to current size pilots 1/4/7 and every entry in the 36 sheet. Attached twig foliage and uneven upper leaders maintain openings through the shrub, replacing spherical leaf volumes. The selected asset is an understory shrub, not the mature single-trunk holly tree form. Spring evergreen foliage has no modeled red winter fruit. Individual spines and waxy reflections are below the geometry/current material representation; the 85 mm leaf envelope is retained. Heights approximately 1.7-3.75 m. Accepted the architecture as a stylized forest holly source; detailed species color treatment remains separate.",
